narrative:
I just disputed this account listed below that showed up on my credit report it caused me much anger and disbelief to see this inaccurate and unverifiable information your agency didn't ensure to be remove from my report but instead just update it. By law I own the right to obtain the steps that were taken to verify this account on my report by your agency. 

XXXX XXXX Date opened : XX/XX/XXXX Status : Closed. {$60.00} past due as of XXXX XXXX. 
Status updated : XXXX XXXX Balance : {$470.00}

This is not a duplicate nor is this complaint being filed by a third party, I am filing this complaint myself. Please see this complaint is processed to the letter of the law. 

We've talked to the bank & they've agreed to remove the account. BUT TransUnion has some internal block which they're claiming they can use to not block the account because they feel they're above the law. When questioned why they're not accepting the Identity Theft report they claim they have an internal policy ( which is OUTSIDE FCRA laws ) & they're unwilling to explain why they won't accept the Identity Theft report ( which is a FEDERAL LAW ). So TransUnion feels they're above the letter of the law & will not explain their policy... 
XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Date Opened : XX/XX/2015 Balance : {$1000.00}

This is the third time I have filed a complaint with Experian. I have asked TWO times for them to verify the accuracy of this account in accordance to my fair credit reporting rights and they have NOT done so and verify it as VALID. I also have not received the data I have asked for under my rights to see HOW the account was verified. They fave failed to report accurate and true information and I DEMAND the removal of this account. 
It is illegal for Experian to report this account as being charged off ( C/O ) month after month starting XX/XX/XXXX to today. This inherently re-starts the statute of limitations and is violating my consumer rights. Also their reporting is significantly different than the reporting of XXXX data. I demand this be removed immediately or I will hire legal counsel and sue. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Account number XXXX Opened XX/XX/XXXX {$7900.00}

