This is a formal complaint against the claim that was denied on my account. 
I received an email from Bank of America on XX/XX/2022 advising me about a fraudulent transaction. I immediately called the bank to report the fraudulent transaction. this was the time when I was made aware that there were fraudulent charges on my debit card. Several days later I received a letter from Bank of America informing me that my claim was denied because they think i gave permission to someone else to use my debit card. I called the bank of america to have my claim reevaluated and i was told to write a letter to the claim department which I did in a timely manner. I went to the Bank of America to get the letter faxed.I was told by the branch manager that he faxed and that I don't have to worry because my card offers me zero liability for fraud. severals weeks later i received another letter from bank of american stating that my reevaluation was denied again and there is nothing they can do. i explained to them that i need this case to be fixed because im recovering from a bad year due to the pandemic and need my money back.they said no and hang out. Also, they failed to send proof of purchase to see who did the purchase. 

Fraudulent transactions are the following : XXXX for {$3900.00} XXXX XXXX {$150.00}

I Have Chase Saving & Checking account. I also have a Chase Credit Card. I manage all XXXX  accounts at the same site. 
I Pay my MONTHLY Credit card balance on this site where the Money is deducted from my Chase Checking account immediately. I have just noticed that Chase now representing this Credit card Payment as a LOAN PAYMENT on their website. I have taken no Loan from Chase and the Credit Card payment SHOULD NOT be listed as Loan payment. 


Date Description Type Amount Action XX/XX/XXXX Payment to Chase card ending in XXXX XX/XX/XXXX Loan  payment - {$1100.00}

Good evening I have tried using my virtual AMEX gift card at multiple merchants online and most have accepted the card as a payment method, but could not complete my purchase. The balance is slowly drained from constant pre-authorization charges after linking. I have spoken on the phone-line and even participated in multiple forum threads to find an acceptable merchant, but there has been no luck. At this point, I am just paying XXXX cents every time to test whether the card would link to a merchant or not. 

This has been a frustrating and unforgiving experience for the constant inconveniences. I would like the rest of the funds to be mailed as a check to me, and I will not be touching any of the funds anymore. 

